+   c. Compute the axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) extents of the projected Gaussian in screen pixels. The extents along the screen x and y axes are $\sigma_{x,i} = k \sqrt{\Sigma'_{i,xx}}$ and $\sigma_{y,i} = k \sqrt{\Sigma'_{i,yy}}$, where $k$ is a confidence factor (typically 3) [G].
+   d. Determine the maximum axis length: $L_{max, i} = \max(\sigma_{x,i}, \sigma_{y,i})$.
+   e. If $L_{max, i} > \tau_\lambda$, discard Gaussian $i$ [S1].
+   f. Otherwise, keep Gaussian $i$ for rendering [S1].
 
